        "original_id": "0537c54d-9c82-5491-b7d5-0c2ddf5ed2da",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Paul Cook, Matthew Ashman, Samuel Gluckstein, Barnett Salmon\n- Bands and Companies: Sex Pistols, Chiefs of Relief, Salmon & Gluckstein\n- Places: Hammersmith, London, UK\n- Topics: punk rock, electro-punk, tobacco retail\n\nFacts:\n- Barnett Salmon and Samuel Gluckstein founded Salmon & Gluckstein in London in 1873.\n- Salmon & Gluckstein expanded to become the largest tobacco seller in the UK, with over 140 retail outlets.\n- The Sex Pistols formed in London in 1975 as an English punk rock band.\n- Paul Cook was born on 20 July 1956 in Hammersmith, London.\n- Paul Cook is an English drummer and a member of the Sex Pistols.\n- Chiefs of Relief were a British rock group with an electro-punk style.\n- Chiefs of Relief featured guitarist and vocalist Matthew Ashman and drummer Paul Cook.",
